# Deliberate divergences. libSQL's Hrana transport releases a sqld namespace
# when its last connection closes, so the conformance tests must close every
# connection they open; leaving one open leaks the namespace for the whole run.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/JSON1Test.java -- Hrana holds a namespace until its last connection closes, so the conformance copy closes the leaked per-test connections.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/CachedRowSetTest.java -- Hrana holds a namespace until its last connection closes, so the conformance copy closes the leaked connection and asserts the row it reads.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/InsertQueryTest.java -- upstream misuses the connection factory so the transaction is applied to a different connection and never asserts the result; the conformance copy reuses the transaction connection, asserts rollback and commit visibility, and asserts the final count (#51).
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/PreparedStatementThreadTest.java -- upstream swallows every ExecutionException, which hides assertion failures and runtime exceptions from the close/execute race; Hrana serializes requests per stream, so the conformance copy awaits both futures and tolerates only an SQLException cause, and any runtime failure fails the test as the Java equivalent of the native crash it guards (#51, #118).
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/DBMetaDataTest.java -- sqld rejects CREATE TEMP TABLE with SQL_PARSE_ERROR, so the conformance copy skips only columnOrderOfgetTables on libSQL and leaves the xerial control run intact.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/StatementTest.java -- Hrana sends one statement per Stmt so sqld rejects multi-statement strings (SQL_MANY_STATEMENTS), sqld rejects CREATE TEMP TABLE (SQL_PARSE_ERROR), and Hrana streams are independent so DROP succeeds while a materialized result set is open; the conformance copy skips those cases on libSQL. xerial's DATE-millis round trip is replaced on libSQL by the java.sql date-only value, and the copy uses standard JDBC unwrap and closeOnCompletion calls plus drops the sqlite-jdbc-only generated-keys configuration hook so it compiles without the xerial classes.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/PrepStmtTest.java -- Hrana has no describe request, so the conformance copy skips the parameter-type, pre-execution metadata, and pre-execution SQL-validation expectations on libSQL, and uses the java.sql date-only value instead of xerial's DATE-millis round trip; it also reassigns the result set after the next execute as java.sql requires and drops the cases that call sqlite-jdbc's own configuration and error-code classes.
